## Local stack with Docker Compose

```sh
docker compose -f docker-compose.otel.yml up --build
```

The compose file runs this server with the OpenTelemetry Java agent on http://localhost:8080/fhir next to `grafana/otel-lgtm`, which holds Grafana on http://localhost:3000, Prometheus, Loki, Tempo, and an OpenTelemetry collector that gets the signals of the server. The stack publishes port 8080 and, by default, the ports 3000, 4317, and 4318 on the host, and its Grafana gives admin access with no login, so use it only on a machine that others cannot reach.

The build argument `OPENTELEMETRY_JAVA_AGENT_VERSION` pins the agent to <%= agentVersion %>. Keep the argument, because with an agent that is older than the instrumentation API of this server, every route stays at the servlet mapping `/fhir/*`.

If another stack holds port 3000, 4317, or 4318, set `LGTM_GRAFANA_PORT`, `LGTM_OTLP_GRPC_PORT`, or `LGTM_OTLP_HTTP_PORT` to a free host port.
<% } -%>
