## nx serve with the agent

```sh
nx serve <%= projectName %> --otel
```

The `--otel` flag downloads the OpenTelemetry Java agent <%= agentVersion %> to `target/opentelemetry-javaagent.jar` with `mvn dependency:copy` and starts the server with the agent and `OTEL_JAVAAGENT_CONFIGURATION_FILE=otel/agent.properties`, unless you set that variable. This setup includes no collector. Run a collector at http://localhost:4318, or set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`. For a local Grafana LGTM stack, run this from the project root. It publishes the ports 3000, 4317, and 4318 on the host, and its Grafana gives admin access with no login.

```sh
docker run --rm -p 3000:3000 -p 4317:4317 -p 4318:4318 \
<% if (dashboard) { -%>
  -v "$PWD/otel/grafana/dashboards:/otel-lgtm/dashboards:ro" \
  -v "$PWD/otel/grafana/provisioning/dashboards:/otel-lgtm/grafana/conf/provisioning/dashboards:ro" \
<% } -%>
  grafana/otel-lgtm
```
<% } -%>
